  "productionInventorySha256": "17c0b90f171b7a27ff4aa710c19567eb6d7438877a5c6e1c3c7eb6f97331dcdf",
  "inventoryReview": "Classified the new LongValues/LongValueVisitedSet.cs as traversal-owned bounded identity storage for CopyPayloadAsync, with direct generated capacity/probe calls included in implementation review. The existing deallocation tracker and all other production source names remain unchanged.",
  "reviews": [
    {
      "boundary": "implementation",
      "obligations": "Reviewed generated null/budget admission and positive bounded payload consumption before each CopyPayloadAsync output effect, checked casts/counter headroom, release-before-next-acquisition and preserved malformed/single-page error priority. Reviewed lazy 16-slot visited-table allocation, half-occupancy doubling, bounded circular probing, duplicate refusal before growth and exact rehash membership manually. Reviewed the explicit caller-stream live I/O, failure/disposal and exclusive-access contract against direct FileStream classification and custom-stream rollback. Existing journal/replacement codecs, shared range/read and serialized writer-lifecycle mappings retain their separate payload, authority and returned-I/O contracts.",
      "conformance": "LongValueTraversalTests independently checks collision/growth membership, cycles before reacquisition, no-progress refusal and wide slice/count boundaries; LongValueStreamingTests and LongValueStoreTests retain cancellation, partial output, release and existing format behavior. PageStoreTests, LeaveOpenTests, StatementSpillTests, JetTransactionTests and WriterLifecycleConformanceTests bind the live-stream contract. ReplacementCleanupConformanceTests and RecoverableWriterLockTests supplement the new multi-client model with removed-name, competing-handle, retry, stale-owner and exact-evidence controls. Exact build/test execution receipts and settled-main CI verdicts are reported separately.",
      "remainingAssumptions": "The traversal model bounds aggregate uint-array payload allocations and logical page-prefix acquisition work; CLR overhead/GC, locator/cache/pool and destination resources remain separate. Exact handwritten table membership/rehash is manual correspondence with independent tests, not an automatic C# proof. Returned I/O, immutable borrowed bytes, cryptographic identity, snapshot effects, canonical coordination, stale-I/O fencing, OS locks and physical persistence remain contracts. Non-FileStream callers retain live rollback only; stream disposal can itself persist buffered bytes. No complete public parser, arbitrary concurrent C# correctness or caller-stream persistent recovery claim is admitted.",
