    {
      "boundary": "proof-trust",
      "obligations": "Reviewed the exact eight-model inventory and normal-source LongValueTraversal-to-LongValueKernel dependency, native traversal/count/capacity/probe additions and unchanged generated projection, Dafny 4.11.0/bundled-Z3 and compiler/runtime pins. LongValueTraversal proves distinct visits, decreasing budgets, bounded probes and cumulative allocation under named row/write effects. MultiProcessOwnership proves arbitrary finite multi-client trace invariants, historical current-ticket authority, crash revocation and constructive fresh/recorded acquisition and cleanup schedules; checked counterexamples cover premature coordinator release and stale pathname deletion. Mandatory source policy, audits, negative controls, generated freshness and failed-input retention remain unchanged.",
      "conformance": "The dedicated traversal and multi-client mapping documents identify production invocations, independent malformed/membership tests and the exact successful-effect/manual correspondence boundaries. The caller-stream contract separates current live rollback from future journal/reopen/lease capabilities. Existing focused proof-review, verifier-tooling and formal-workflow regressions pass; final exact-source proof/audit/freshness receipts and all settled-main CI runtime/library, analyzer and consumer verdicts are reported separately.",
      "remainingAssumptions": "The pinned verifier/solver, native-source projection, C# compiler, runtime and host remain trusted; no new assumption, admitted lemma, external declaration or shipping dependency is introduced. Multi-client Coordinate assumes atomic canonical exclusion; complete missing-destination composite acquisition and ordinary held-handle disposal are not mechanically refined by the retained-database cleanup schedule. Actual OS exclusion, lock-rank/deadlock prevention, physical namespace/device durability and whole-parser refinement remain separate. Receipt freshness does not attest reviewer identity or judgment.",
